# 2. Scope

## Purpose

This section defines the scope of the engineering objectives established within this System Objective Specification (SOS).

It identifies the intended boundaries of the AVIA system objectives, ensuring that subsequent requirements, architectures, and engineering activities remain aligned with the defined purpose of the system.

---

## Scope Statement

The System Objective Specification defines the objectives that the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) system is intended to achieve throughout its operational lifecycle.

The scope includes the identification of solution-independent system objectives that describe the desired capabilities, behaviors, and performance outcomes of the AVIA system without prescribing implementation methods.

---

## In Scope

The SOS includes:

- Definition of system objectives.
- Identification of desired system capabilities.
- Definition of intended system behaviors.
- High-level operational performance objectives.
- Objective relationships and traceability.
- Objective-level engineering constraints and assumptions.
- Alignment with the approved Project Charter.

---

## Out of Scope

The SOS does not include:

- Detailed system requirements.
- Engineering architectures.
- Hardware selection.
- Software design.
- Algorithms.
- Control logic implementation.
- Mathematical models.
- Physical component design.
- Verification procedures.
- Validation procedures.

These subjects shall be addressed within their respective engineering documents.

---

## Scope Boundary

The SOS serves as the authoritative definition of **what the AVIA system must achieve**.

It intentionally avoids defining **how the system will achieve those objectives**, preserving engineering flexibility for subsequent design, analysis, and implementation activities.
